     7	> P5P6 and bridge modules re-run at `DepthK = 5` with `MaxTime` and the
     8	> other bounds sized so that every registered witness still fires, or
     9	> (b) a written argument … that every checked invariant is independent
    10	> of the value of `DepthK`". This is path (a). No committed module or
    11	> configuration is edited; every run here uses a copy of the committed
    12	> `.tla` and a derived `.cfg` kept beside its `.out` in this directory.
    13	> Every `.out` was produced by TLC 2026.07.31 with `-deadlock` (as the
    14	> committed runs are, since the models stop at `MaxTime` by design);
    15	> vacuity runs used `-continue` and `scripts/filter-tlc-output.sh`.
    16	
    17	## 1. P5c issuance protocol (`P5c_IssuanceProtocol.tla`, unchanged)
    18	
    19	**What changed between instances.** Only constants. The committed
    20	instance is `MaxTime = 14, Delta = 3, DepthK = 2, MaxAttempts = 3`
    21	(k = 3). `DepthK = 5` is k = 6 (`DepthK = k − 1`, A2 §A2.1).
    22	
    23	**Finding first: the window must exceed the depth, or shipping is
    24	unreachable in the instance.** `Ship` requires `depth >= DepthK` and
    25	`now <= declared + Delta` together (module lines 260–263); depth
    26	grows by at most one per `Tick`, so an instance with `Delta < DepthK`
    27	cannot ship at all. This is a property of the finite instance, not of
    28	the protocol: the registered parameters have δ = 72 h against six
    29	confirmations of roughly an hour, so δ ≫ k there. The reading aid's
    30	item 20 recorded that `DepthK = 2` is not the registered default; it
    31	did not record that raising `DepthK` alone breaks the instance. The
    32	two runs below show it.
    33	
    34	| Instance | Main cfg (six invariants + `RefusalLatched`) | Sanity cfg (seven witnesses must all fire) | Evidence at k = 6? |
    35	|---|---|---|---|
    36	| `Delta = 3, MaxTime = 17, DepthK = 5` (`P5c_k6_d3.*`) | green, 3387 distinct states | **only four fire**: `RefusalUnreachable`, `RefusalWithLiveAnchorUnreachable`, `RefusalBuriedAnchorUnreachable`, `RefusalAfterReorgUnreachable`. `ShipUnreachable`, `ReissueShipUnreachable`, `ReorgShipUnreachable` **survive**: no state ships | **No.** `NoShippedOrphan`, `ShippedIsSound`, `ExpiredCannotShip` hold vacuously. Recorded as the negative control for the bound |
    37	| `Delta = 6, MaxTime = 26, DepthK = 5` (`P5c_k6_d6.*`) | green, 9099 distinct states, 16363 generated, 0 on queue | **all seven fire** (one violation block each in the filtered `.out`) | **Yes.** |
    38	
    39	`MaxTime = 26` is the module's own rule, `MaxAttempts · (Delta + 1) +
    40	DepthK = 3 · 7 + 5`, applied at the new constants (module header lines
    41	93–97; the committed 14 is the same rule at `Delta = 3, DepthK = 2`).
    42	
    43	**Companions at the k = 6 instance** (`Delta = 6, MaxTime = 26, DepthK = 5`):
    44	
    45	| Companion | Registered expectation | Observed |
    46	|---|---|---|
    47	| `P5c_IssuanceProtocol_Broken` (`_Broken_k6.*`) | red on `NoShippedOrphan` | red on `NoShippedOrphan` (first violation at 172 distinct states). *Correction 2026-09-14 (Codex qualification (b)):* the run stops at the first violation, and the `_Broken` module defines only `NoShippedOrphan` (its committed cfg lists that one invariant), so "red on exactly" is not a claim this companion can make or the committed record makes; "red on the one invariant it carries" is the statement |
    48	| `P5c_IssuanceProtocol_BrokenSilent` (`_BrokenSilent_k6.*`) | red on `NoSilentDeadlock` | red on exactly `NoSilentDeadlock` (3857 distinct states at the violation) |
